<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Durham Castle</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1072">1072</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Durham Castle is a Norman castle in Durham, north-east <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, begun in 1072 on the orders of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-the-conqueror">William the Conqueror</a>. For centuries it was the residence of the prince-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> of Durham, who governed the county palatine from it. Since 1837 it has housed University College of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/durham-university">Durham University</a>, and with the cathedral it forms a World Heritage Site.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/durham-castle.jpg" alt="Durham Castle" width="320" height="198" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Benjamin Smith · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Durham_-_Views_from_the_central_tower_of_the_cathedral_-_04.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
